<!--
  Hebrew for ui/tutorial/ — the first-run guided tour.

  ⚠️ THE BUCKET IS `values-iw`, NOT `values-he`. See values-iw/strings.xml for
  the measurement; HebrewLocaleResourceTest fails the build if a `values-he`
  directory appears.

  WHY THIS EXISTS WHILE #51 IS DEFERRED

  It is not a resumption of #51 and it opts nothing in. `HebrewLocaleResourceTest`
  is APP-WIDE, not sweep-scoped: its `every translatable english string has a
  hebrew counterpart` case reads every file in values/ and fails on any key with
  no counterpart here. So the moment a new res/ file is authored — which
  ui/tutorial did, because authoring 24 strings in res/ costs the same keystrokes
  as authoring them inline and this is the one moment at which that is true — its
  Hebrew is owed by the build, today, and not by #51.

  `Observed:` 2026-08-22, rather than assumed. Moving this file out of the tree
  and re-running that class gives `7 tests completed, 1 failed`, naming every key
  below. Worth measuring because the alternative reading — that the guard is
  scoped to the swept packages, like `AnalyticsLiteralSweepTest` — is the obvious
  one, and under it this whole file is dead weight added during a freeze.

  Nothing renders it: AppLanguage.OFFERED still excludes HEBREW, so this is
  parked infrastructure exactly like values-iw/analytics_strings.xml. When #51
  resumes, this package is already done.

  The two wording rules it follows (kb/dev/untranslatable-idioms.md §3–§5):

  1 · TERMINOLOGY (§5.1 / E1): the `Goal` entity is יעד, NEVER מטרה — matching
      values-iw/strings.xml and values-iw/components_strings.xml.

  2 · NO HEBREW PREFIX ATTACHED DIRECTLY TO A DIGIT RUN (§4.8). tutorial_step_counter
      keeps a space on both sides of each specifier (שלב %1$d מתוך %2$d), so the
      bidi algorithm resolves the digits as their own run and the Hebrew words
      stay where they were written. `ב%1$d` would land on the far side of them.

  Register matches the rest of the app: plural imperative (הקישו, בחרו), never
  masculine singular.
-->
